From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:27:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 78/91] Doomsday range and hold, passive and automated
 targeting

- Doomsdays have no range limit; the target only has to stay locked.
- A titan that fires its doomsday is held in place for effectDeactivationDelay
  (30s). The destiny manager lets it go when the time runs out.
- Passive targeters start a silent lock on activation (TargetSilently). The
  target isn't told, doesn't see it in its targeter list, and npc AI doesn't
  react to it.
- Automated targeting systems are fitted as active modules again. At the end of
  each cycle they lock the nearest hostiles within targetHostileRange (rats, and
  pilots you can shoot without a crime), up to your free target slots.
